# Strategy B (REALTIME_MOMENTUM_V1) FSM/setup/entry/exit rules checksum, declared before any B backtest result.
# canonical: sha256 of json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":"), ensure_ascii=False) UTF-8
#            = app.backtest.strategy_c_selection.rules.canonical_checksum (existing US-B recipe)
# file:      sha256 of the file bytes (informational; the canonical value is the gate)
# declared:  (superseded, see below) 2026-09-19 19:09 KST (final), repo main HEAD a2b91ee
# results:   0 B backtest runs existed at declaration time. B had no FSM, no setup detection and no entry code
#            when the first draft was written, and none of the three drafts read B data or produced a B result.
# revision:  two earlier drafts of the same session were superseded while the FSM was being written:
#            18:51 KST  d6063e17024df2fd79a1eb475ca46ef918e7bf333719d8688eb577d9a6e297ff
#                       -> SETUP_READY became a per-tick re-evaluation: the trigger is judged before the
#                          close-below-stop invalidation (a bar that breaks out and then fails is a taken loss,
#                          not a cancelled setup), a setup that merely disappears falls back to WATCHING, and the
#                          signal-then-fill tick order was written down.
#            19:05 KST  94d5a13689d0438dc101b4c68582ad0b11bf1aa4afb94e5fc796c7903549e928
#                       -> eligibility is rechecked in every non-terminal state, ahead of the TTL check, so an
#                          ENTRY_SIGNALLED candidate can still be REJECTED (an inferred halt stops the entry).
# declared:  2026-09-20 11:52 KST (final), repo main HEAD a2b91ee
#            2026-09-20  288cd7e308393e52b23e82518d185d0c46ce5cbdd73a7316cd2160d89097760c
#                       -> the exit layer was implemented and its open details were written down while
#                          still at zero results: the exit scan starts at the entry bar, HARD_STOP vs
#                          TRAILING_STOP is decided by whether the stop has moved, a partial that rounds
#                          to zero shares closes the whole position at the target, a deadline fills at the
#                          last close before it, sizing only lowers for the position cap, and CON is
#                          recorded as a universe exclusion (Windows reserved path name).
